course: dictionary
lesson: 1901
title: Colossal and the power of big words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Colossal» means extremely large, huge or enormous. In «Deeper down live the colossal squid», the clue is that the squid is a giant animal, so colossal means very big.
explain: The word can also mean very great in amount or degree. In «a colossal mistake», nobody thinks the mistake is the size of a house. It is a very big mistake, and the writer uses colossal to make it sound bigger.
explain: The word comes from the Colossus of Rhodes, a giant statue in the ancient world and one of the Seven Wonders. When you meet a big word, ask yourself whether it is meant literally (really huge) or for effect (very great).
fact: «Colossal» means extremely large, huge or enormous.
fact: «Colossal» can also mean very great in amount or degree, as in «a colossal waste».
fact: The colossal squid has the largest eyes known of any animal, about 27 cm across.
fact: The colossal squid lives in the deep Southern Ocean and is the heaviest animal without a backbone known.
fact: Giant squid live deep in the dark sea, so they are rarely seen by people.
exercise: «Colossal squid have the largest eyes known of any animal.» What does colossal mean here? | Very quiet | *Extremely large | Bright red | Very old
exercise: Mia says, «That was a colossal mistake!» What does colossal mean in this sentence? | *A very great, very big mistake | Wet and cold | Very small | Covered in ice
exercise: Which word means about the same as colossal? | Slow | Tiny | Quiet | *Huge
test: Where does the colossal squid live? | In a shallow pond | *In the deep Southern Ocean | On a high mountain | In a hot desert
test: The word colossal comes from a famous statue. What was it called? | Eiffel Tower | *Colossus of Rhodes | Statue of Liberty | Great Pyramid
exam: Which sentence uses colossal to mean very great in amount? | «The colossal statue stood in the square.» | «The colossal squid has huge eyes.» | «The colossal whale swam past the boat.» | *«The party cost a colossal amount of money.»
